{{Infobox LGBT rights|location_header=Sanyan|image=Sanyan map.png|imagesize=250px|caption=|legal_status=Never illegal|gender_identity_expression=Anyone can change their registered gender without surgery. "{{W|Intersex}}", "{{W|third gender}}" and "{{W|Non-binary}}" always recognized|recognition_of_relationships=Never regulated (All {{W|free love|forms of marriage}}, such as {{W|polyamory}} / {{W|group marriage}}s recognized)|adoption=Never restricted|military=LGBTQ+ persons allowed to serve openly|discrimination_protections=Sexual orientation and gender identity protection}}'''LGBTQ rights in Sanyan''' are some of the [[LGBTQ rights in Kaftia|most advanced in Kaftia]]. 

For centuries, there has been widespread acceptance and embracing of diverse sexualities and [[W:Gender identity|gender identities]]. Sanyanian society has never viewed gender as a binary in the way that it is predominately seen in the [[W:Western World|Western World]], nor did they correlate anatomy to gender identity. As a result of Sanyan's resistance to [[Illypnian colonialism|Western colonialism]] and [[W:Imperialism|imperialism]], there has never been any persecution of LGBTQ individuals because of their sexuality ("imported homophobia"), nor any anti-LGBTQ laws. 

The legal status of these rights is formally established in the [[Basic Law of Sanyan]], which prohibits discrimination on the basis of both [[W:Sexual orientation|sexual orientation]] and [[W:Gender identity|gender identity]] in all areas (housing, employment, education, and access to public services). Full legal recognition is granted to all forms of committed relationships, including [[W:Same-sex marriage|same-sex marriage]] and [[W:Polyamory|polyamorous unions]]. Furthermore, legal gender recognition is based purely on [[W:Self-determination|self-determination]], requiring no medical or psychological requirements.  

Sanyan's national ideology, ''[[Obodo àlàáfíà]]'' (communal wellbeing), ensures state support and positive rights for the LGBTQ+ community. Under the country’s extensive welfare state, the free [[W:Universal health care|universal health care]] system includes comprehensive coverage for [[W:Gender-affirming care|gender-affirming care]]—including hormonal therapies and surgeries—as these are considered essential components for promoting individual autonomy and communal wellbeing. The national education system integrates curricula on sexual and gender diversity across all compulsory grades, framing these topics within the context of traditional Sanyanian history to encourage early destigmatization. In foreign affairs, Sanyan is an active global advocate for LGBTQ+ rights, especially within Kaftia, using its diplomatic influence and its [[W:State media|state-backed media]] group, [[Noya]], to support and shelter [[W:LGBTQ migration|LGBTQ+ refugees]], as an extension of its Pan-Kaftian and anti-colonial alignment.

